WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.140
Привет, Фрэнс, welcome to привет, русский эпизод 20-ть, 4-21-я мая-26-го года.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.920
I'm Olya, and we've got some great Russian word to learn today.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.440
Поехали, let's go.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.280
Today's word of the day is солнце, солнце.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.460
Repeat after me, солнце, it means sun.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.440
Imagine the sun as a big round-soul, warming everyone up.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.820
Today the sun is shining, солнце светит сегодня.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.500
Now you can describe a bright morning in Russian.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.000
Now that you know солнце, let's learn more weather words.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.600
The next word is дождь, repeat after me, дождь, it means rain.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.200
Think of drizzle, but shorter and bouncer.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.560
It is raining, идет дождь.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.960
This word helps you notice when plants might need to move indoors.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.180
Our next word is жара, repeat after me, жара.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.440
It means heat, it sounds like jaunt, but hotter.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.060
In summer there is strong heat, let them be white, сильная жара.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.120
Knowing жара, let's you explain why you want extra water or shade.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.480
Let's add ветер, repeat after me, ветер.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.280
It means wind, wet, lack of a ternarian, who helps animals on a windy day.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.820
A strong wind is blowing, do it, сильный ветер.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.740
With this word you can talk about why leaves or kites fly so high.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.260
Next comes oblaka, repeat after me, oblaka.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.860
It means cloud, oh boy, a fluffy cloud.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.440
There is a white cloud in the sky, в небе белая облака.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.360
You can now point at the sky and name what you see.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.840
Now try снег, repeat after me, снег, it means snow.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.940
Snow снегs up quality, snow falls in winter,

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.320
зимой падает снег.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.940
This word connects you to winter games and causes indoor days.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.480
Our last weather word is гроза, repeat after me, гроза.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:52.340
It means thunderstorm, гроза, like gross a big storm with thunder,

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:55.200
a loud thunderstorm, громкая гроза.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.820
It prepares you to describe the dramatic sky safely from inside.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.340
One more gentle word is тепло, repeat after me, тепло.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.020
It means warm, tap like tap it but cause you're.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.940
It is warm outside, на улице тепло.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.360
In Russian we often say weather this way, we say на улице,

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.120
followed by the weather word.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.540
It is like saying the whole air feels a certain way.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.380
На улице жарко means it is hot outside,

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.760
на улице холодно means it is cold outside.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.080
На улице тепло means it is warm outside.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.080
You just made your first weather sentence in Russian.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.460
Russian love talking about the weather.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:38.440
Their country has long snowy winters and short hot summers.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.120
People often ask,

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.980
«Готовая страна?»

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.620
or stay inside with tea and books.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.120
Let's practice now.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.220
Do you remember what song some means?

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.400
Can you say it again?

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.400
Look out the window and try.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.940
На улице with one of our new words.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.700
Say three times with different words if you like.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.140
For the kids at home,

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.400
draw a picture of the sun or clouds

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.860
and say each Russian word while you point.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.580
Now, here's something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.380
Did you know the Russian word

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.740
« температура»

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.360
and the English word « температура»

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.760
are actually the same word?

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.920
They both come from the Latin word

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.580
for a balance of heat and cold.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.540
The word traveled through Europe

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.040
and entered Russian in the 1700s.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.080
But watch out.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.420
Жара sounds a bit like жар,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.120
yet it means intense heat, not a container.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.700
Next time you check the temperature on your phone,

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.380
remember it shares a root with температура

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.360
about balancing hot and cold.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.720
That connection is your secret shortcut.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:40.480
Молодец.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.240
That means well done.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.160
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.360
Practice saying today's words out loud even just once

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.480
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.700
See you next time.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:52.060
Пока!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.740
That's Russian for bye.

